{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478755-stands-in-cofd","id":1478755,"title":"Stands in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-13T06:07:05-07:00","id":1478755,"title":"Stands in CofD","content":"Was watching a bit of JoJo\u2019s Bizarre Adventure with my brother a few days ago, and have been struck with these two (2) inquiries since;<br /> <br /> 1. How would each splat (be they canon or fan-made) react to a stand-user and their stand?<br /> <br /> 2. How would a fight between a supernatural and, say, Jotaro, go?<br /> <br /> Note that the supernatural in question would be \u2018maxed out\u2019, with their Power Stat and Attributes being at ten (10), their Energy Stat being similarly filled, and having all applicable (and legal) merits and maximised Skills.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Jotaro (I\u2019ll be using him out of convenience) would <i>also</i> be at his most powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T10:47:09-07:00","id":1478776,"title":"","content":"1) Depending on how new the supernatural is to the supernatural, somewhere between confusion to &quot;Fifty shades of the same ol' shit&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) The general rule of Stands is that they can do one thing, but do it very well and very creatively. Star Platinum something of an odd exception, but we'll come around to it.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing that has to acknowledged is that the Jojo's Bizarre Adventure canon is a battle action shonen manga/anime series that has it's roots in horror, where as Chronicles is an urban horror RPG, so the rules by which powers and combat works differently from each other-explicitly, Chronicles is incentivized to avoid fights in favor of either overwhelming force, harrying, controlling the field, etc., etc., ie pretty tactical approaches to combat to a point where fights either don't even happen, happen only shortly, or last in a prolonged state under great duress for all involved, where Jojo's is incentivized to have big, flashy, up and in in each other faces battles, where sneaking up on someone may give you an advantage, but just as often is a way to introduce a particular quirk of the character's personal abilities or Stand manipulation.<br /> <br /> What this generally means is that even the quirkiest and most subversive Stand-users tend to be tankier than the usual character in Chronicles. Jotaro Kujo and his Stand are <i>not</i> quirky and subversive, by contrast-in fact, Star Diamond's &quot;singular&quot; ability is to be so physically perfect that it actually can do many things very well, up to and including reacting fast enough to allow Jotaro, at his upper limits, to use SD as a mini-time stop (a mini ZAWURDO, for the fans). It's hard to <i>snipe this guy</i>.<br /> <br /> By contrast, almost any protagonist of Chronicles that has gotten to the heights of their power can do <i>a lot of things</i> really well, but they're still horror protagonists in a game where having a straight fight is a sucker's game.<br /> <br /> So you can almost reduce this question down to &quot;how much overwhelming violence can they commit against Jotaro without actually getting into a fight?&quot; As a general rule, skirmishes with enemies that Jotaro are unlikely to kill but can push to reveal the limits of Star Diamond might happen, but either with or without, then said supernatural either hits them with their best bet to just wipe the page, which in a lot of cases would also mean city-wide destruction.<br /> <br /> And at the extreme high end of power, pretty much every supernatural except <i>maybe</i> Deviants can manage to pull that off. Some of them might need to be throwing their cults left and right at them, and as a standard rule, mages, mummies, demons, and certain vampires are gonna have to resort to less than everyone else, but basically everyone can do that.<br /> <br /> If you get into an actual fight with Jotaro Kujo, particularly at his heights, you're facing a losing fight-Star Diamond is just too physically powerful. Make it not a fight, and Jotaro loses, the question is if beating Jotaro is worth the costs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Star Platinum, not Star Diamond. Star Diamond is a Revue Starlight thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-13-2022, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T14:24:56-07:00","id":1478792,"title":"","content":"As far as reactions go, the only real point I can think of is that Sin-Eaters and Beasts would likely have a greater interest in Stands simply because of their own status as similar entities where two being are bonded together. Beasts especially would likely be very interested in forming a Kinship bond with a stand user and see if they can learn to harness their Horror in new ways. Plus a Stand user like Jotaro is headed pretty quickly for Apex territory anyway.<br /> <br /> As far as fighting Jotaro? You don't. He's a physical powerhouse. Nobody in the CofD is designed to go toe-to-toe with someone like him as Arc has well covered. Jotaro's biggest weakness is that he has no innate powers to stop mind or fate manipulating powers. CofD powers also frequently do not have the loopholes or quirks that Jotaro normally manages to figure out to avoid losing to such foes in the JJBA-verse. A lot of JJBA fights between physical Stands and manipulative Stands come down to the physical Stand user have to endure a lot of pain to buy time to figure out whatever oddities define the manipulative Stand's powers and then find a way to twist that to their advantage.<br /> <br /> In JJBA, when Jotaro has to deal with someone that can accurately predict the future with their Stand, that comes with a downside that said Stand User has no idea what happens between now and that point in the future, and thus as long as that single prophecy event comes true, anything else is fair game. A maxed out Acanthus mage doesn't have to worry about that sort of restriction and can doom Jotaro to a horrible fate that he has no real ability to avoid other that having really high natural resistance Attributes to Withstand magic with. A maxed out Dominate vampire just orders Jotaro to Ora! Ora! Ora! himself into paste rather than try to fight him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T16:24:04-07:00","id":1478804,"title":"","content":"There was a point where Stands were explained as alternate manifestations of the Ripple/Hamon, which in turn channels the power of the sun. This was scrapped pretty quickly, but if it returns (or just grant Stand Users access to the Ripple too), they\u2019d have\u2026 <i>interesting</i> relationships with the Stone Masks and Pillar Me\u2014 I mean, Kindred.<br /> <br /> Any Stand User would be a valuable packmate to the Uratha, who may view them as superpowered Wolf-Blooded of a sorts\u2026 or Claimed, in which case relations might become edgy. Still, the likes of Jotaro fighting toe-to-toe with Uratha in Gauru form likely earns them respect.<br /> <br /> Aaaannd I gotta go now, with the usual disclaimer and acknowledgement that mages (especially ones Obsessed with psychic and Astral phenomena) would have a field day with all the Mysteries that Stand Users generate and tend to meet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T15:05:48-07:00","id":1478975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478755-stands-in-cofd?p=1478776#post1478776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Star Platinum, not Star Diamond. Star Diamond is a Revue Starlight thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks. I'm not completely familiar with all of the Stands in JJBA, so I can't always keep them straight.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to remind you all that I used Jotaro as an <i>example</i> character of sorts, so you're completely welcome to use others in his place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}